[{:db/id "q-102304/selection/4463792f6934aa25bb2e783377f9224e69e3d339df1d001ee7956d364a8577aa" :answer/id #uuid "0f1ddf92-3419-5130-9a50-5a478e600b02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{12(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102304/selection/7e5edfdceb13564712c2eeebc39919d0258a9c58506bec45a0363c2d8d4212b7" :answer/id #uuid "d01b0f44-cfa0-5791-b7c5-1ff0a154c9bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=12{a}_{n}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102304/selection/9401a5b5b6a1a466f774f832578a493e704cf7be41fbc50afcc18adf71238a9d" :answer/id #uuid "b2f1bf81-cb4f-54ed-bb5f-06086f7c6d84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{3{a}_{n}}{(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102304/selection/bc958269065c48c0599b917e231c924c9af01a01a1d2246a76cf1294e18cbf01" :answer/id #uuid "049cf688-ebd9-58c9-8635-b3f7e0af4380" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102304/selection/71b3114253383b64dbaace06f68b84408b1cbadfb78ff887b07ee5088c834fad" :answer/id #uuid "d6070e63-a296-5ced-8a35-479e789d1069" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{(4n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102304/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "144be257-7345-54c9-a5a8-1cdd34e8c412" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102304/selection/bc958269065c48c0599b917e231c924c9af01a01a1d2246a76cf1294e18cbf01" :answer-field/choices ["q-102304/selection/4463792f6934aa25bb2e783377f9224e69e3d339df1d001ee7956d364a8577aa" "q-102304/selection/7e5edfdceb13564712c2eeebc39919d0258a9c58506bec45a0363c2d8d4212b7" "q-102304/selection/9401a5b5b6a1a466f774f832578a493e704cf7be41fbc50afcc18adf71238a9d" "q-102304/selection/bc958269065c48c0599b917e231c924c9af01a01a1d2246a76cf1294e18cbf01" "q-102304/selection/71b3114253383b64dbaace06f68b84408b1cbadfb78ff887b07ee5088c834fad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102304" :question/id #uuid "ff5a4452-7358-5569-954f-338c9c8a6546" :question/math-academy-id "q-102304" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $4y+12{y}^{′}=0.$ \n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=0,1,2,…?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+12{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the second sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+12{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the second summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+12{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[4{a}_{n}+12(n+1){a}_{n+1}]{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n4{a}_{n}+12(n+1){a}_{n+1}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)},\\,n=0,1,2,….\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102304/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d058486e-3e14-5649-815a-7730311c5aec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102304"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101381/selection/2d4dfc66b2585a0d28578acc752e9386d7b090989a2317dd476c8f44bbac6b66" :answer/id #uuid "f19f8ec1-bc62-5f59-af3c-85bc4d90ba36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-12{a}_{n}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101381/selection/abcfa59c143031e794690949005f45d097ed45648327b9c47dcdc7f37089c2d4" :answer/id #uuid "85021ec1-3345-5816-878e-b8f7bc3b2ad3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=4{a}_{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101381/selection/70b3a88316ea76119ee579697544c7ae0ebce7e3458365a8c00ecf3cdd690c01" :answer/id #uuid "c853958f-241f-55ad-aa67-e095d8e08b70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{4{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101381/selection/f1aebb2e99feb4351f3b28a6d01d2f1a56b6ddb5cd895133320512f10682d622" :answer/id #uuid "1501873c-d3d3-552f-af5a-163a4af170e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{4{a}_{n}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101381/selection/c2d059a906dfe6335fa918beeb8d1845b69351bb0be82e0db3b67bd3676e8981" :answer/id #uuid "3af091e8-0110-5873-8ba2-360fa711cd20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{12{a}_{n}}{(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101381/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "29e0027d-ad5b-5d1b-b87c-5afa4dd7fa26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101381/selection/70b3a88316ea76119ee579697544c7ae0ebce7e3458365a8c00ecf3cdd690c01" :answer-field/choices ["q-101381/selection/2d4dfc66b2585a0d28578acc752e9386d7b090989a2317dd476c8f44bbac6b66" "q-101381/selection/abcfa59c143031e794690949005f45d097ed45648327b9c47dcdc7f37089c2d4" "q-101381/selection/70b3a88316ea76119ee579697544c7ae0ebce7e3458365a8c00ecf3cdd690c01" "q-101381/selection/f1aebb2e99feb4351f3b28a6d01d2f1a56b6ddb5cd895133320512f10682d622" "q-101381/selection/c2d059a906dfe6335fa918beeb8d1845b69351bb0be82e0db3b67bd3676e8981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101381" :question/id #uuid "ac34c253-b1a1-583e-93d2-70299030c461" :question/math-academy-id "q-101381" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $3{y}^{′}-4y=0.$ \n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=0,1,2,…?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}-4{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}-4{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-4{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[3(n+1){a}_{n+1}-4{a}_{n}]{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n3(n+1){a}_{n+1}-4{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{4{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)},\\,n=0,1,2,….\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-101381/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d058486e-3e14-5649-815a-7730311c5aec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64512/selection/069eaa3d9f6c083465047afbaaa32d72f851c6ed0b42c1110048cb34de9a0a12" :answer/id #uuid "26b527b5-adf6-5f2f-8b8c-efa8c0d64562" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-3(n+1){a}_{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64512/selection/47e891caf556354c724046b7462130f99e94e2bc01e4cecfc1babc43d06a3828" :answer/id #uuid "b253da26-16a7-5cb8-9363-f458554706b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n}+3}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64512/selection/490cfd8ed8d2dff7dfdf05b136715234e6ad40e95066bd014ed545a384eea182" :answer/id #uuid "6ef98098-9e1e-50d9-a3ac-98b0901d95f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{3{a}_{n}}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64512/selection/2ce4f482a94cc57a476b708ebe63123504bb6a10f745f2d517cc696ada4afd47" :answer/id #uuid "a26f8da3-ef62-596f-94c2-2519b6a46952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{3n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64512/selection/e4c9097960a92bf0071425a4cbf9da1464847d97e0a02ed8d1cc6162efd87c30" :answer/id #uuid "b8f9179e-68bd-56b9-b994-868b6b6c0b00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64512/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "703f6183-06e8-5349-b8b0-1d7afaf43b90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64512/selection/e4c9097960a92bf0071425a4cbf9da1464847d97e0a02ed8d1cc6162efd87c30" :answer-field/choices ["q-64512/selection/069eaa3d9f6c083465047afbaaa32d72f851c6ed0b42c1110048cb34de9a0a12" "q-64512/selection/47e891caf556354c724046b7462130f99e94e2bc01e4cecfc1babc43d06a3828" "q-64512/selection/490cfd8ed8d2dff7dfdf05b136715234e6ad40e95066bd014ed545a384eea182" "q-64512/selection/2ce4f482a94cc57a476b708ebe63123504bb6a10f745f2d517cc696ada4afd47" "q-64512/selection/e4c9097960a92bf0071425a4cbf9da1464847d97e0a02ed8d1cc6162efd87c30"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64512" :question/id #uuid "966dd0c9-cf07-546a-9c89-a8e149239b59" :question/math-academy-id "q-64512" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $3{y}^{′}-y=0.$ \n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=0,1,2,…?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[3(n+1){a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}]{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n3(n+1){a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)},\\,n=0,1,2,….\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64512/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d058486e-3e14-5649-815a-7730311c5aec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64512"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365775/selection/b6fc63a121e34801a0ac746ecc8504ef5efd5815c3f81170a53fc8da6edd9531" :answer/id #uuid "ee3f0981-f75e-5e4b-8b79-61193c4107d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-5{a}_{n}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365775/selection/738659f55839e053a086315302e8f45ec2b62b19ace8f4ed0dfa23d04c8f3919" :answer/id #uuid "b6536593-e426-5c91-a402-0587cd017904" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{5{a}_{n}}{n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365775/selection/16531d768aa0362e07cf82efa92bcebb115fc3aff860f635b2afd236c3e6e7a6" :answer/id #uuid "7437e0ac-9f00-5b85-ba45-a606c7eda790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{5{a}_{n}}{n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365775/selection/86d60fe867a71b8349b656723d7662b1240309e7c88a6eaaac81701ba18ff2eb" :answer/id #uuid "2fe01dbf-9faa-527e-a232-7319de277085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-5n{a}_{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365775/selection/a761605ce4bcb29369c35d2fb855b2320253669c753c6942603c2d7c18089ca5" :answer/id #uuid "c7c91b12-a221-5a24-99fc-abfbcdb237d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{5(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365775/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2db850f-1e0c-5d89-89ee-3d979077f544" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-365775/selection/16531d768aa0362e07cf82efa92bcebb115fc3aff860f635b2afd236c3e6e7a6" :answer-field/choices ["q-365775/selection/b6fc63a121e34801a0ac746ecc8504ef5efd5815c3f81170a53fc8da6edd9531" "q-365775/selection/738659f55839e053a086315302e8f45ec2b62b19ace8f4ed0dfa23d04c8f3919" "q-365775/selection/16531d768aa0362e07cf82efa92bcebb115fc3aff860f635b2afd236c3e6e7a6" "q-365775/selection/86d60fe867a71b8349b656723d7662b1240309e7c88a6eaaac81701ba18ff2eb" "q-365775/selection/a761605ce4bcb29369c35d2fb855b2320253669c753c6942603c2d7c18089ca5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365775" :question/id #uuid "b6d4f7db-2063-514e-8996-30801ae185d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-365775" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation ${y}^{′}+5y=0.$ \n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=0,1,2…?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+5{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+5{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+5{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[(n+1){a}_{n+1}+5{a}_{n}]{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n(n+1){a}_{n+1}+5{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{5{a}_{n}}{n+1},\\,n=0,1,2….\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365775/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d058486e-3e14-5649-815a-7730311c5aec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365775"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365781/selection/2b2f8380f6caeeb88cda61c856eb30bbadd6e365278a9532ac63a92d64b6a996" :answer/id #uuid "55e9d8b9-5abf-5a47-9cf7-a75f0fd6b62d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=4{a}_{n}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365781/selection/60ca5fbd32df1e22acacad13d488124b30dc059933c207bacb34f866edef6909" :answer/id #uuid "c1d0cc7c-2e0f-5b74-9951-f1b28788e3ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{4(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365781/selection/6befeedf05fc4d805a3232e4dc73a4cc5085d8a77cfdb7bf6810c9963b9e66d3" :answer/id #uuid "25f05ca5-ec8f-5618-a78f-1a80b88d239a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{4n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365781/selection/030c88223713b9d2fbf7279fd135e4950f2b7739a4dfc23d8413967c6383dffd" :answer/id #uuid "2c83a90d-2bcf-536c-be80-ff9343f38354" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{4{a}_{n}}{n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365781/selection/ff2ab5e9df194c0a307415258f46bef56e854cd1dae051f8dce7ada7ff5ee204" :answer/id #uuid "9c294c2f-f774-5bd7-a2cf-667e60119684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{4(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365781/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4333941-fa0c-576c-b1ba-55e261ceeb98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-365781/selection/60ca5fbd32df1e22acacad13d488124b30dc059933c207bacb34f866edef6909" :answer-field/choices ["q-365781/selection/2b2f8380f6caeeb88cda61c856eb30bbadd6e365278a9532ac63a92d64b6a996" "q-365781/selection/60ca5fbd32df1e22acacad13d488124b30dc059933c207bacb34f866edef6909" "q-365781/selection/6befeedf05fc4d805a3232e4dc73a4cc5085d8a77cfdb7bf6810c9963b9e66d3" "q-365781/selection/030c88223713b9d2fbf7279fd135e4950f2b7739a4dfc23d8413967c6383dffd" "q-365781/selection/ff2ab5e9df194c0a307415258f46bef56e854cd1dae051f8dce7ada7ff5ee204"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365781" :question/id #uuid "951aa831-fbe3-556e-b499-16fb98fc86cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-365781" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $4{y}^{′}-y=0.$ \n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=0,1,2…?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[4(n+1){a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}]{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n4(n+1){a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{4(n+1)},\\,n=0,1,2….\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365781/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d058486e-3e14-5649-815a-7730311c5aec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102312/selection/572e0a644385d59ecc793174bf479b79409ad0daf27a32e0133da4f262acebca" :answer/id #uuid "d423ad7f-d69c-513f-a7e3-daef2fa77942" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{2{a}_{n-1}}{3n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102312/selection/fa6d7e70c4837eb155bf05982806bca2161ef8ee8996eefbb5d5df772b089c2d" :answer/id #uuid "5313a7ae-be7b-538f-a191-d586773a9d3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{2(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102312/selection/74d825dcda91766bda012d957dbd22467119e5aa5f360398b9dd76bf7027c1ec" :answer/id #uuid "4b789450-69bf-5553-a729-52977f536449" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-6{a}_{n-1}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102312/selection/8cbedba1c564c441778047e94bcc74310548e4d6c593d7be4b77017e7bae806e" :answer/id #uuid "683fc09b-f4f3-5e57-a1f7-ea87223c616f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{2n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102312/selection/d539206fcd6f7427ff97a7a8417293be773d3fb7b6e4a6436a2a7f8b0a89feb7" :answer/id #uuid "4d3f57b8-15ca-579a-942b-d51270659a6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-5{a}_{n-1}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102312/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23ee027e-b6dd-56fa-a575-375b3c007d48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102312/selection/fa6d7e70c4837eb155bf05982806bca2161ef8ee8996eefbb5d5df772b089c2d" :answer-field/choices ["q-102312/selection/572e0a644385d59ecc793174bf479b79409ad0daf27a32e0133da4f262acebca" "q-102312/selection/fa6d7e70c4837eb155bf05982806bca2161ef8ee8996eefbb5d5df772b089c2d" "q-102312/selection/74d825dcda91766bda012d957dbd22467119e5aa5f360398b9dd76bf7027c1ec" "q-102312/selection/8cbedba1c564c441778047e94bcc74310548e4d6c593d7be4b77017e7bae806e" "q-102312/selection/d539206fcd6f7427ff97a7a8417293be773d3fb7b6e4a6436a2a7f8b0a89feb7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102312" :question/id #uuid "17d14283-fdda-5f13-b86f-e9cd3b8d6301" :question/math-academy-id "q-102312" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $3xy-2{y}^{′}=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}-2{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the second sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}-{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }2(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }2(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}-2{a}_{1}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n-2{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[3{a}_{n-1}-2(n+1){a}_{n+1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,2(n+1){a}_{n+1}=3{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{2(n+1)},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-102312/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ab3f10-aca4-5094-98d2-0de9c11fd711"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102312"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64536/selection/359db202ff2dc12a1469101dd5fffb7e4acceb1277fcb11d6a6ca8e465616ae4" :answer/id #uuid "804642e8-626d-5770-9537-9d0a993fdd90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-7(n+1){a}_{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64536/selection/0b4c6961a5d90bc53f9cfab02954a73ab7598fca1d488fc3ee669465b5107a54" :answer/id #uuid "71dad90f-280e-5dee-9ce4-e5faaa1ff6e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=7n{a}_{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64536/selection/239e1bb2c53b28c069923aa9339f55d5644271439fac871eba4ead65d1a7c134" :answer/id #uuid "0c618fa7-b080-5c03-970f-00f749c6aaf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-7n{a}_{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64536/selection/c99f045214b0a988f85278c8001e71f6e80b8253b8550bb9300eb8963fffdc3f" :answer/id #uuid "5a1dbfcf-f094-5db6-a78f-8d2e204ab2bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{7(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64536/selection/d4cafec6b1faadb643fef81203f8db1bc1d4d3654786b52a3cd6e2e714b8a1bc" :answer/id #uuid "320295b1-f16a-58cc-a443-623b6e5bf185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{7{a}_{n-1}}{n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64536/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cdcc0029-6c41-5f3d-87ce-0cfdf54aaf58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64536/selection/d4cafec6b1faadb643fef81203f8db1bc1d4d3654786b52a3cd6e2e714b8a1bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-64536/selection/359db202ff2dc12a1469101dd5fffb7e4acceb1277fcb11d6a6ca8e465616ae4" "q-64536/selection/0b4c6961a5d90bc53f9cfab02954a73ab7598fca1d488fc3ee669465b5107a54" "q-64536/selection/239e1bb2c53b28c069923aa9339f55d5644271439fac871eba4ead65d1a7c134" "q-64536/selection/c99f045214b0a988f85278c8001e71f6e80b8253b8550bb9300eb8963fffdc3f" "q-64536/selection/d4cafec6b1faadb643fef81203f8db1bc1d4d3654786b52a3cd6e2e714b8a1bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64536" :question/id #uuid "410df22e-fae0-5291-8e4b-8ae39b283772" :question/math-academy-id "q-64536" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation ${y}^{′}+7xy=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+7x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+7{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+7{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the second series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+7{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+7{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+7{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[(n+1){a}_{n+1}+7{a}_{n-1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,(n+1){a}_{n+1}=-7{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{7{a}_{n-1}}{n+1},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-64536/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ab3f10-aca4-5094-98d2-0de9c11fd711"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64536"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102317/selection/985409f7ffa70bfd83ee8b98a2d224b097b21b6184138a1e04036d086bdd9c37" :answer/id #uuid "5300a6f7-1edd-5f11-94e0-61fdc5ef6652" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102317/selection/9cb1e4eafe9b7f6f0f84b02561e8f3e9d6fd83f5fd565151191302cf00bf73a2" :answer/id #uuid "fef616b0-7436-53be-9a81-8a018e7e6be3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{3(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102317/selection/d174ddc0f6b945fc06d1ec4b31b43b8ac56474aa994e74bac942e812dd12ca07" :answer/id #uuid "aa2db70a-8906-5abe-a0c8-dd5e811be64f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{(3n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102317/selection/bf5872ef7442bcb0a50b13843c13d6a3a50e0226f584c142c8e38a177bceb4f7" :answer/id #uuid "d7b77e40-ff8a-5f6a-815c-fdcf50dcf24f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=3{a}_{n-1}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102317/selection/f7b626085a6234e472731203a8016365b9a365c75b7474cb90771266bc51c48e" :answer/id #uuid "35d99852-1c78-5917-b55a-4ae00e1ee5d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-{a}_{n-1}(3n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102317/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a7598a7-4351-5eda-86e6-59b96de7b3c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102317/selection/985409f7ffa70bfd83ee8b98a2d224b097b21b6184138a1e04036d086bdd9c37" :answer-field/choices ["q-102317/selection/985409f7ffa70bfd83ee8b98a2d224b097b21b6184138a1e04036d086bdd9c37" "q-102317/selection/9cb1e4eafe9b7f6f0f84b02561e8f3e9d6fd83f5fd565151191302cf00bf73a2" "q-102317/selection/d174ddc0f6b945fc06d1ec4b31b43b8ac56474aa994e74bac942e812dd12ca07" "q-102317/selection/bf5872ef7442bcb0a50b13843c13d6a3a50e0226f584c142c8e38a177bceb4f7" "q-102317/selection/f7b626085a6234e472731203a8016365b9a365c75b7474cb90771266bc51c48e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102317" :question/id #uuid "b23fe339-e5a3-520f-aea5-79137303ca56" :question/math-academy-id "q-102317" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $6xy+2{y}^{′}=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+2{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }6{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the second sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }6{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}+{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }2(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }6{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }2(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}+2{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n2{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[6{a}_{n-1}+2(n+1){a}_{n+1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,2(n+1){a}_{n+1}=-6{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{(n+1)},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-102317/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ab3f10-aca4-5094-98d2-0de9c11fd711"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102317"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101402/selection/a3264b7b32c2a73d525264a7034f4eb7b684bd37f7a3c9b5500532990eedabc7" :answer/id #uuid "5eb0cc05-e490-5139-9c90-9fd43de5461f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-{a}_{n-1}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101402/selection/910a5d47a37d6460f0f532bc58c47c4a1df7f4b14ecfcf0e25612ef12db466a1" :answer/id #uuid "6ce5b765-6e95-5b58-a615-7d8f2d0beb92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{2n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101402/selection/e7efeb78b328490a3179a1f8140ec157d35bc82f0ab069a4229f34e4ed7cf780" :answer/id #uuid "77b01364-5fc3-5673-8848-4dea5c0bb829" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{2(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101402/selection/25687c4903f0602494eb4c2d8ecce6251e3e1ef32f3be4636728f80e9bad32d6" :answer/id #uuid "5e2335c9-6bf5-56d4-b4cb-65880c59866a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101402/selection/10b724726f484e83cdbb9681127d6fdcb287df281b114c8b7a2835323cc0c7fa" :answer/id #uuid "62f962da-53c8-5127-8f00-512a091dfd2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101402/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f7a4ef0-2bcc-5936-b05d-5797ef983519" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101402/selection/e7efeb78b328490a3179a1f8140ec157d35bc82f0ab069a4229f34e4ed7cf780" :answer-field/choices ["q-101402/selection/a3264b7b32c2a73d525264a7034f4eb7b684bd37f7a3c9b5500532990eedabc7" "q-101402/selection/910a5d47a37d6460f0f532bc58c47c4a1df7f4b14ecfcf0e25612ef12db466a1" "q-101402/selection/e7efeb78b328490a3179a1f8140ec157d35bc82f0ab069a4229f34e4ed7cf780" "q-101402/selection/25687c4903f0602494eb4c2d8ecce6251e3e1ef32f3be4636728f80e9bad32d6" "q-101402/selection/10b724726f484e83cdbb9681127d6fdcb287df281b114c8b7a2835323cc0c7fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101402" :question/id #uuid "c4b94f8d-a475-55bb-bec7-595ae4adc188" :question/math-academy-id "q-101402" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $6{y}^{′}+3xy=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+3x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }6(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the second series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }6(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }6(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n6{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n6{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[6(n+1){a}_{n+1}+3{a}_{n-1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,6(n+1){a}_{n+1}=-3{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{2(n+1)},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-101402/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ab3f10-aca4-5094-98d2-0de9c11fd711"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101402"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64541"] :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $4{y}^{′}+xy=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }4n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }4(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the second series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }4(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }4(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }4(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[4(n+1){a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n-1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,4(n+1){a}_{n+1}=-{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{4(n+1)},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-101385/selection/d29c61adb2f89dd371a3c12fecf134140c6fb124186c894588a2d72ef3eaa31f" :answer/id #uuid "bd5c3009-85a9-5ff5-a0f2-371c2b3c9461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{2}{3n(n+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101385/selection/6f3ef05909080f6c212f68b71ed3058468ebaf8c5fa15b55eae63a00a6aca857" :answer/id #uuid "77c5420c-2488-5f62-9deb-2060ca669c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{(n+1)(n+2)}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101385/selection/70d72442450522b43e49940d972909447d62b8e81fea82a1357718ee5f1a202f" :answer/id #uuid "c90b606c-5d71-532f-a2f4-29c32b715a6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{2}{3(n+1)(n+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101385/selection/0c1f59cf35fa88d0b4b5e1468ad33022e3af1ea7794ad8ab3956b8a502c02816" :answer/id #uuid "6c5d0022-e547-5ed1-b625-6399cec56f9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{3(n+1)(n+2)}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101385/selection/53a6141fdb1badfe65f343bf38a0d62db7c6a7639e71e71aebf54d2592256e83" :answer/id #uuid "31d2b2b9-0b14-510a-8b86-ebad695dcb37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{3n(n+1)}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101385/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "63e2365f-25a8-5496-bf56-3065f105ff0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101385/selection/0c1f59cf35fa88d0b4b5e1468ad33022e3af1ea7794ad8ab3956b8a502c02816" :answer-field/choices ["q-101385/selection/d29c61adb2f89dd371a3c12fecf134140c6fb124186c894588a2d72ef3eaa31f" "q-101385/selection/6f3ef05909080f6c212f68b71ed3058468ebaf8c5fa15b55eae63a00a6aca857" "q-101385/selection/70d72442450522b43e49940d972909447d62b8e81fea82a1357718ee5f1a202f" "q-101385/selection/0c1f59cf35fa88d0b4b5e1468ad33022e3af1ea7794ad8ab3956b8a502c02816" "q-101385/selection/53a6141fdb1badfe65f343bf38a0d62db7c6a7639e71e71aebf54d2592256e83"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101385" :question/id #uuid "df28548c-91d7-53ca-be69-ef2a161ac056" :question/math-academy-id "q-101385" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $3{y}^{″}-2y=0.$  Find $f(n),$ given that the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{f(n)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find ${y}^{″}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}-2{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}-2{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}-2{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[3(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-2{a}_{n}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n3(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-2{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{2{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=\\frac{3(n+1)(n+2)}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-101385/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1980ddeb-37bf-5234-8888-f8292e2c9405"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101385"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102309/selection/4cb971bff65142b660c97fb2c8aaf7850b36d4da40c01022c018cc4925a75684" :answer/id #uuid "56226db1-0b12-5d9d-9ac6-51269caeaffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-6(n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102309/selection/a374b688d02543058192798fef53300c1859c18a393286344387ad50b06b8e1b" :answer/id #uuid "d63470cd-c0e5-5bbb-b15a-4c275349c0e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{2(n+1)(n+2)}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102309/selection/f04cd1ba4092e5f02993a05bfdc5f542e89fdb14b3b9848075a425ca7be4c616" :answer/id #uuid "0f43337a-c15a-57f5-a55f-0ceb4656a2bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{3(n+1)(n+2)}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102309/selection/fef2d349cc4aee5ce52bcea22e7b1576538bfd267c8350520d4f8819287eb2cd" :answer/id #uuid "266767e3-5192-5cf1-b5b4-6792ee0223d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{2}{3(n+1)(n+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102309/selection/edfd96b89610513cd6aea31a1425d377d38978b236c74da3de46703ca12fad2f" :answer/id #uuid "9d24b7b6-7fb4-525d-a76f-a6d79a1b7b31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-(2n+1)(3n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102309/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5833c098-1ce1-5bf4-b430-b140c6dd9142" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102309/selection/f04cd1ba4092e5f02993a05bfdc5f542e89fdb14b3b9848075a425ca7be4c616" :answer-field/choices ["q-102309/selection/4cb971bff65142b660c97fb2c8aaf7850b36d4da40c01022c018cc4925a75684" "q-102309/selection/a374b688d02543058192798fef53300c1859c18a393286344387ad50b06b8e1b" "q-102309/selection/f04cd1ba4092e5f02993a05bfdc5f542e89fdb14b3b9848075a425ca7be4c616" "q-102309/selection/fef2d349cc4aee5ce52bcea22e7b1576538bfd267c8350520d4f8819287eb2cd" "q-102309/selection/edfd96b89610513cd6aea31a1425d377d38978b236c74da3de46703ca12fad2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102309" :question/id #uuid "77f6137f-8b9e-50aa-8326-ee49fc392f6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-102309" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $6y+9{y}^{″}=0.$  Find $f(n),$ given that the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{f(n)},\\,n=0,1,2,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find ${y}^{″}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n6{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+9{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the second sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n6{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+9{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the second summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n6{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+9{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[6{a}_{n}+9(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n6{a}_{n}+9(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=-\\frac{2{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=-\\frac{3(n+1)(n+2)}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102309/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1980ddeb-37bf-5234-8888-f8292e2c9405"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102309"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64531/selection/90416971b1fc8621e0d7e3f3e37206682e5b4b97a60fd11622e0025a7fd66645" :answer/id #uuid "324aa07a-a79a-50ca-a282-6966c9a15158" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-3n(3n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64531/selection/69fb10651b690f4b7c736d6d26fcab92d62688fa9e7ce51b9f4b932639639881" :answer/id #uuid "d2a78034-d04d-5bf2-92de-eacbf4e23d5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-n(n+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64531/selection/f82fced4a1fb0e85992e7b081c946cf9ab6e2c958e0aa7f69a3bc1e13dd7399e" :answer/id #uuid "8acd55b2-407f-5637-810e-b977ac1dd1a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=n(2n+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64531/selection/cdee8c26c81543d8ca414fc82f95d1a503ead2e728452bce40aa832bdacd2266" :answer/id #uuid "045588b0-7288-5a91-9d78-5fcbcfc05ed8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=3(n+2)(n+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64531/selection/01b3a4d80f95c20445629941be8e3d3099ff25870f296055be6134c6dededfe8" :answer/id #uuid "38613dba-7e75-52bc-8e63-ae8a21f22187" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-3(n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64531/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "86b841a0-6081-523b-8721-72c7e84cda0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64531/selection/01b3a4d80f95c20445629941be8e3d3099ff25870f296055be6134c6dededfe8" :answer-field/choices ["q-64531/selection/90416971b1fc8621e0d7e3f3e37206682e5b4b97a60fd11622e0025a7fd66645" "q-64531/selection/69fb10651b690f4b7c736d6d26fcab92d62688fa9e7ce51b9f4b932639639881" "q-64531/selection/f82fced4a1fb0e85992e7b081c946cf9ab6e2c958e0aa7f69a3bc1e13dd7399e" "q-64531/selection/cdee8c26c81543d8ca414fc82f95d1a503ead2e728452bce40aa832bdacd2266" "q-64531/selection/01b3a4d80f95c20445629941be8e3d3099ff25870f296055be6134c6dededfe8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64531" :question/id #uuid "bb00de42-236c-5869-bf37-8a4664305356" :question/math-academy-id "q-64531" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $3{y}^{″}+y=0.$  Find $f(n),$ given that the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{f(n)},\\,n=0,1,2,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find ${y}^{″}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[3(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}+{a}_{n}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n3(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}+{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=-3(n+1)(n+2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64531/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1980ddeb-37bf-5234-8888-f8292e2c9405"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64531"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365780/selection/ac5e2dd68f1a4a62102e21441cd92f236c22fff689007724ab2028187c35f335" :answer/id #uuid "8878390e-be7b-5904-ad7b-bed01e2f8369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=3n(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365780/selection/841249340240705fdbd431ed5bf01aaf5e534a5bff899fdb5d58ef09a6043ad1" :answer/id #uuid "5e3fe36a-68bf-5d0f-bfe9-5cc3c6aeb9ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=3(n+1)(n+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365780/selection/2a2015ea9a5c349504149cf552f9cb288a30e085c199515231c7b078c40b3277" :answer/id #uuid "646b1a3c-f711-5e2b-b9f9-0af425c82ab0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=3(n+1)(2n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365780/selection/5e31d58fbec2f9375b891c9cec6839a1b160e388a40f81d638aed839b76dbd8a" :answer/id #uuid "448c83d1-121b-5f7f-a5d2-1e420a901f80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=3(n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365780/selection/2300cd686be51b6a37f3871fa55151dc20ede5c7887a20947631f652409bed88" :answer/id #uuid "4f4749c1-d25d-5b58-acec-6e0f52ff6cb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=(n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365780/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "93e60e72-c4c2-5a45-988a-50b9506b6a73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-365780/selection/5e31d58fbec2f9375b891c9cec6839a1b160e388a40f81d638aed839b76dbd8a" :answer-field/choices ["q-365780/selection/ac5e2dd68f1a4a62102e21441cd92f236c22fff689007724ab2028187c35f335" "q-365780/selection/841249340240705fdbd431ed5bf01aaf5e534a5bff899fdb5d58ef09a6043ad1" "q-365780/selection/2a2015ea9a5c349504149cf552f9cb288a30e085c199515231c7b078c40b3277" "q-365780/selection/5e31d58fbec2f9375b891c9cec6839a1b160e388a40f81d638aed839b76dbd8a" "q-365780/selection/2300cd686be51b6a37f3871fa55151dc20ede5c7887a20947631f652409bed88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365780" :question/id #uuid "035a71b2-43f1-5331-8a34-23bb98ad68e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-365780" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $3{y}^{″}-y=0.$  Find $f(n),$ given that the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{f(n)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find ${y}^{″}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[3(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-{a}_{n}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n3(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=3(n+1)(n+2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-365780/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1980ddeb-37bf-5234-8888-f8292e2c9405"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365780"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102307/selection/e9b3dd838b52442132933d29ee3761a11d494b3bd52fa407dd4d5e433d83f41b" :answer/id #uuid "ac45d126-6a9c-58d3-a64f-0c9409bb3c19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{1}{(n+1)(n+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102307/selection/08ad603389cf528b7615d2911712c7c6f4b31b794ff843bb04cdb22bfedbb1b3" :answer/id #uuid "4d6ef4d2-c301-5294-a992-c5c6687434d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-(n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102307/selection/d8ea0f9574c89f85c5d4e461c6e72ec416cee53626ff8f94d853217d2d9ef6de" :answer/id #uuid "2676b077-1d2e-5511-b74c-cc2b2464f8e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-(2n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102307/selection/3581517e3a1de6da5bcc2700302011c61647578b5b34f0a63b51fa3046043b06" :answer/id #uuid "6bb241d9-48b8-56d7-bce5-4b82a37d692d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{1}{(n+1)(n+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102307/selection/2300cd686be51b6a37f3871fa55151dc20ede5c7887a20947631f652409bed88" :answer/id #uuid "8e3cd709-33c6-5cca-8e51-327038495ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=(n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102307/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ced13391-0ed6-5f15-aa4d-b3705637054e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102307/selection/08ad603389cf528b7615d2911712c7c6f4b31b794ff843bb04cdb22bfedbb1b3" :answer-field/choices ["q-102307/selection/e9b3dd838b52442132933d29ee3761a11d494b3bd52fa407dd4d5e433d83f41b" "q-102307/selection/08ad603389cf528b7615d2911712c7c6f4b31b794ff843bb04cdb22bfedbb1b3" "q-102307/selection/d8ea0f9574c89f85c5d4e461c6e72ec416cee53626ff8f94d853217d2d9ef6de" "q-102307/selection/3581517e3a1de6da5bcc2700302011c61647578b5b34f0a63b51fa3046043b06" "q-102307/selection/2300cd686be51b6a37f3871fa55151dc20ede5c7887a20947631f652409bed88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102307" :question/id #uuid "26bebd5f-bd47-51cf-9d35-830618cac2ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-102307" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $y+{y}^{″}=0.$  Find $f(n),$ given that the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{f(n)},\\,n=0,1,2,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find ${y}^{″}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the second sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the second summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[{a}_{n}+(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}+(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=-(n+1)(n+2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102307/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1980ddeb-37bf-5234-8888-f8292e2c9405"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102307"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6671"] :question/problem "Let $y = \\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n}$ be a series solution to the equation $y'-3y=0$.\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients $a_n$, where $n=0,1,2, \\ldots$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $y'(x){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and $y'(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty n a_n x^{n-1}-3\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n = 0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m = n-1$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\sum_{m=0}^\\infty (m+1) a_{m+1} x^{m} -3 \\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n =0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty (n+1) a_{n+1} x^{n} -3 \\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n =0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0$, we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-3{a}_{n}{x}^{n}] & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[(n+1){a}_{n+1}-3{a}_{n}]{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n(n+1) a_{n+1}  -3 a_n = 0.\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} =\\dfrac{3 a_n }{n+1}, \\qquad n= 0,1,2, \\ldots\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6673"] :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042594/assets/2ad87a5ee9c27f6d3f03b098b804613d81bc91bb5a811b7655e12efcb052f1e8.png) be a series solution to the equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042594/assets/5379e686b1ac80c3cb5fec6c41ae2e281b7db590044ff70ff9c3068ac1332f98.png)\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042594/assets/527b41b4ced63af6b53983c8aee27c21a7651f52abd01b7600d4e2a1102db63f.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042594/assets/6ce3483e55b55dee0411597e321facef4f770900e379d1f82da2ceaf278ef40c.png)?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042594/assets/29dbde1998029c25aedffc9dccb1bbaf47781dc5816a69da0256952d82009ef0.png)\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-wo